# Project-local npm config for code-oz.
#
# Override the user-level @tuel scope mapping to point at the public
# npm registry. The user's ~/.npmrc routes @tuel/* to GitHub Packages
# for the TUEL AI org's private packages; code-oz is published openly
# under @tuel/code-oz on public npm, so we route this scope back to
# registry.npmjs.org for this project only.
#
# Without this file, `npm publish` from this directory would target
# GitHub Packages (where `tuel` is unauthenticated) instead of public
# npm (where `tuel` IS authenticated). The first publish attempt on
# 2026-05-12 hit this routing bug; this file is the durable fix.
@tuel:registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
